  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Neighbourhood policing, tougher action on antisocial behaviour, and a Serious Organised Crime Agency; tougher gun/knife controls, supervision and tagging to cut reoffending; ID cards to combat fraud/illegal working; immigration controls including a points system, English requirement for settlement, biometric visas/e‑passports, and employer penalties; commitment to maintain the nuclear deterrent, NATO as central, and a referendum on the EU Constitutional Treaty/euro only if tests met. TEXT_C: Opposes ID cards and treats drugs as a health issue; restorative justice focus and community policing; strong pro-asylum rights (allow work/benefits, independent appeals, ratify UN migrant workers convention); disestablish Church of England and curb monarchy’s roles; decommission nuclear weapons and cut defence; extensive environmental/climate justice agenda and localisation.",
